    <div style="margin-left: 290px; padding: 40px; line-height: 1.6; color: #333;">
        <h1 style="color: #007bff;">SQL & Analysis in Data Analytics</h1>
        
        <p>SQL (Structured Query Language) is the backbone of data analytics, allowing analysts to retrieve, filter, and manipulate data stored in databases.</p>

        <h2 style="color: #2c3e50;">Core SQL Commands</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>SELECT:</strong> Retrieves data from a database.</li>
            <li><strong>WHERE:</strong> Filters records based on conditions (e.g., <code>SELECT * FROM table WHERE condition;</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>ORDER BY:</strong> Sorts data in ascending or descending order.</li>
            <li><strong>GROUP BY:</strong> Groups similar data for aggregate calculations.</li>
            <li><strong>JOINs:</strong> Combines rows from two or more tables (INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 style="color: #2c3e50;">Course Modules Overview</h2>
        <p>The Google Data Analytics Certificate covers 8 modules, ranging from foundational data concepts to the final Capstone project, teaching tools like <strong>Tableau</strong>, <strong>Spreadsheets</strong>, and <strong>R Programming</strong>.</p>
        
        <h3 style="color: #2c3e50;">Benefits of SQL Knowledge:</h3>
        <p>Without SQL, professional data analysis is difficult because most business data is stored in relational databases. Learning SQL helps you:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Query large datasets efficiently.</li>
            <li>Clean and prepare data for visualization.</li>
            <li>Generate reports for business insights.</li>
        </ul>
